  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SAVING THE SUMATRAN ELEPHANT IN BUKIT BARISAN SELATAN NATIONAL PARK, INDONESIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE GOAL OF THIS PROJECT IS TO ASSIST INDONESIAN AUTHORITIES IN IMPROVING THE MANAGEMENT OF BUKIT BARISAN SELATAN NATIONAL PARK TO MAINTAIN FOREST HABITAT FOR CRITICALLY ENDANGERED SUMATRAN ELEPHANTS AND OTHER THREATENED WILDLIFE. THE PROJECT S OBJECTIVES FOCUS ON PREVENTING THREATS AND PROTECTING HABITATS AND ELEPHANTS BY: (1) STRENGTHENING NATIONAL PARK MANAGEMENT THROUGH THE INTEGRATION OF SMART (SPATIAL MONITORING AND REPORTING TOOL) INTO RESORT BASED MANAGEMENT (RBM) TO REDUCE FOREST ENCROACHMENT, POACHING, AND OTHER THREATS IN KEY ELEPHANT AREAS AND (2) MANAGING HUMAN-ELEPHANT CONFLICT (HEC) BY STRENGTHENING COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION AND INCREASING GOVERNMENT SUPPORT. PROJECT ACTIVITIES ARE TO: (1) PROVIDE ADVANCED TRAINING TO RANGER TEAMS IN ENHANCED SMART PATROL METHODS (2) PROVIDE TECHNICAL ASSISTANCE TO SEVEN RANGER FOREST PATROL TEAMS (3) CONDUCT SMART-RBM STRATEGY EVALUATIONS TO ASSESS THE IMPLEMENTATION OF THE SYSTEM AND RANGER PATROL EFFECTIVENESS AND STRATEGICALLY PLAN PATROLS TO TARGET HIGH-RISK AREAS (4) MITIGATE HEC WITH A RAPID-RESPONSE WILDLIFE RESPONSE UNIT (5) ESTABLISH AND STRENGTHEN ADDITIONAL COMMUNITY-BASED HEC MITIGATION TEAMS (6) ENABLE DISTRICT GOVERNMENT AND OTHER AGENCIES TO PROVIDE SUPPORT IN HEC MITIGATION INTERVENTIONS AND (7) EVALUATE THE EFFECTIVENESS OF HEC INTERVENTION</narrative>
  </description>
